    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Newton's First Law of Motion is frequently referred to as the Law of Inertia.",
        "When a body moves in a circular path, work done by the centripetal force is always zero because force and displacement are perpendicular.",
        "1 Horsepower (HP) is exactly equal to 746 Watts.",
        "If a person holds a heavy load stationary on their head, the physical work done is zero since displacement is zero."
      ],
      "id": "wfsexfy"
